WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:06.020
Taraja Ramsess, a stunt performer whose film
credits include "Black Panther," "Avengers:

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:12.090
Endgame," and "The Suicide Squad," died on
October 31st in a vehicle collision in Georgia.

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:13.660
He was 41 years old.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:18.810
His four children were also in the vehicle
with him, two of whom also died at the scene,

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:23.440
while his 10-year-old son was placed on life
support, but died shortly thereafter.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.848
The crash happened shortly before midnight
on Halloween night.

00:00:26.848 --> 00:00:32.254
"They say that he was on his way home when
his truck and an eighteen-wheeler collided."

00:00:32.254 --> 00:00:36.070
Ramsess' mother confirmed the news on Instagram,
writing,

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:39.590
"All who knew and met him know how special
Taraja was.

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:43.720
He had a deep capacity for love and loved
his children more than all.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:49.020
He loved his martial arts, motorcycles and
all things related to filmmaking.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:55.180
He [had] a very droll yet wicked sense of
humor &amp; yet could be as cornball corny as can be."

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:59.340
Director Ava DuVernay released her own statement
to Instagram.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:04.349
Ramsess was a crew member for the "Selma"
filmmaker's distribution company, ARRAY.

00:01:04.349 --> 00:01:05.349
DuVernay wrote,

00:01:05.552 --> 00:01:06.552
"Taraja.

00:01:06.552 --> 00:01:07.439
Regal.

00:01:07.439 --> 00:01:10.140
That's the word that comes to mind when I
think of him.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:11.866
He walked like a king.

00:01:11.866 --> 00:01:14.105
And to me, always acted like one.

00:01:14.229 --> 00:01:16.914
[...] He loved making movies and TV too.

00:01:16.914 --> 00:01:19.265
Held many positions over the years.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:22.170
Immersing himself in all aspects of the craft."

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:26.750
Ramsess' passing is a devastating loss to
the stunt community, with him having helped

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:31.756
bring to life numerous moments from some of
the most popular films of the last several years.

00:01:31.756 --> 00:01:36.119
Ramsess brought his passion for martial arts
into a variety of stunt work for numerous

00:01:36.119 --> 00:01:37.704
high-profile projects.

00:01:37.704 --> 00:01:42.810
His first stunt credit came in 2015 when he
served as a stunt double for Papa Midnite

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:44.810
in an episode of "Constantine."

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:49.520
From there, he appeared in a string of comic
book adaptations, doing stunts for "Black

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:52.710
Lightning," "She-Hulk: Attorney at Law," and
"Black Adam."

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:57.770
He even has some on-camera appearances, as
he appears as a Wakandan soldier in "Avengers:

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:01.085
Infinity War" and a groomsman in “What Men
Want.”

00:02:01.085 --> 00:02:05.299
Ramsess also had experience in the art department
for various productions.

00:02:05.299 --> 00:02:10.030
He's worked as an on-set dresser, who is responsible
for arranging objects on a set before the

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:16.660
cameras roll, on many film and TV sets, including
"The Hunger Games: Catching Fire," "Furious

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:18.710
7," and "What Men Want."

00:02:18.710 --> 00:02:23.550
Looking over his resume, it becomes abundantly
clear that Ramsess was a singular talent who

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:25.840
excelled in many different disciplines.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:30.230
He was a key behind-the-scenes figure who
will be missed by all those who worked with him.

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:34.730
Numerous professionals have populated his
mother's Instagram tribute with kind words

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:38.709
of their own to remember how dedicated Ramsess
was to his craft.

00:02:38.709 --> 00:02:42.879
Fashion designer Tameka Foster empathized
with her situation, posting,

00:02:42.879 --> 00:02:46.560
"As a Mom who has lost a son, my heart breaks
for you.

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:48.850
I am truly sorry for your loss.

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:51.467
I will pray for your grandbabies as well."

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:55.629
Actor Carrie Bernans shared her own special
connection with Ramsess, posting,

00:02:55.629 --> 00:03:00.950
"My deepest condolences [...] He was truly
an incredible person to work with.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:05.760
We worked on the set of Black Panther together
and he's always been such a joy to be around

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:07.590
and full of life and love.

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:09.940
Sending you all so much prayers &amp; love."

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:15.671
Ramsess' passing is a huge loss both for the
entertainment community and his immediate family.

00:03:15.671 --> 00:03:20.420
After his death, a GoFundMe was established
for his mother to help cover any forthcoming

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:27.369
expenses, and has already received more than
$87,000 in donations, as of the making of this video.

